@startuml
' UML Sequence Diagram: Agile Scrum Workflow
' Participants
actor "Product Owner" as PO
participant "Scrum Master" as SM
participant "Developers" as DEV
actor "Stakeholders" as STK

== Backlog Management ==
PO -> PO: Maintain Product Backlog
PO -> PO: Refine & Prioritize Items

== Sprint Planning ==
SM -> PO: Facilitate Sprint Planning
SM -> DEV: Facilitate Sprint Planning
PO --> DEV: Present Product Goal & Top PBIs
DEV -> DEV: Estimate PBIs
DEV -> DEV: Select PBIs for Sprint Goal
DEV -> DEV: Create Sprint Backlog

== Sprint Execution ==
loop Daily Scrum (every day)
  SM -> DEV: Facilitate Daily Scrum
  DEV -> DEV: Plan daily work
  DEV -> SM: Raise impediments
  SM -> SM: Remove impediments
end

par Development
  DEV -> DEV: Implement User Stories
  DEV -> DEV: Unit & Integration Tests
else Code Review
  DEV -> DEV: Peer Code Review
end

alt Meets Definition of Done?
  DEV -> DEV: Verify DoD
  note right of DEV
    Done = Coded, Tested, Reviewed,
    Integrated, Documented as agreed
  end note
else Rework
  DEV -> DEV: Fix Issues and Retest
end

== Review ==
DEV -> SM: Demonstrate Increment
SM -> STK: Facilitate Sprint Review
STK --> PO: Provide Feedback
PO -> PO: Update & Reorder Product Backlog

== Retrospective ==
SM -> DEV: Facilitate Retrospective
DEV -> DEV: Identify Improvements
SM -> SM: Plan Process Improvements

alt Release Now?
  DEV -> PO: Propose Release
  PO --> STK: Communicate Release Plan
else Defer Release
  DEV -> SM: Feed into Next Sprint Planning
end

@enduml
